terests of ordinary working  people who are trying to get by in this  country who need decent pay  decent housing and decent jobs and  it feels to me time and time again that  this conservative party i'm afraid  are governing in the interests of their  wealthy  friends and that's when it gets found  out so  yes it's it's not just about your  processes and whether you've got strong  leadership  and you know i absolutely believe that  kierstarma would have  sacked matt hancock or or if it had been  any one of us in this situation  on the spot and how you deal with them  but it's also about  in whose interests are you governing in  whose interests  are you a politician and that's where  the labour party and the conservative  party  you really have quite a big uh  difference i think  you say the cursed armor would have done  this differently and been decisive and  all that  but look you're confronted with the  government against whom you  can and have made over many months  credible charges of hypocrisy  sleaze cronyism and sheer incompetence  yet you managed to lose a by-election in  a previously  safe seat last month you're in danger of  losing  another one this week and you're way  behind in the polls how can that  possibly be i mean how do you manage  that  well the by-election on thursday has not  happened yet  uh we've got a fantastic local candidate  in kim ledbetter who is a very  passionate local community activist  she's not really a  politician at all and will be fighting  for every vote on  on thursday so let's see what happens uh  there but of course you know in  in a pandemic it's not a time of  politics  as usual people want to see the  government succeed  we want to get back to life as normal  and  we have to take a a slightly different  approach as  as the opposition people don't want to  just hear from  us in terms of opposition for  opposition's sake they want to see us  being  constructive and and working uh where we  need to working with the governm